      {
        "id": 125597,
        "name": "Rabk",
        "username": "Rabk",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabk/{size}/1978_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-08T20:19:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Been trying to think of a way to encourage shifting between styles while also taking emphasis away from tools. A little unwieldy, but it's a start:</p>\n<p><em>Funky Strike</em> (29hp): [<em>You may?</em>] destroy a tool card. If you do, deal 1<span>&nbsp;target 3[<em>2?</em>] melee damage. Otherwise, deal&nbsp;</span><span>1 target 0 melee damage. You may play a style card now.</span></p>\n<p>The thematic fun of jumping in and out of Mantis makes up for any loss of tool/harmony functionality if you ask me.&nbsp; <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/stuck_out_tongue.png?v=9\" title=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":stuck_out_tongue:\"></p>",
        "post_number": 33,
        "post_type": 1,
